# Renault 21 phase 1 saloon, 1986-1989.
#
# The first-generation Renault 21 in its phase-1 form, launched in June 1986 and
# sold in right-hand drive in Britain from the start. The phase-2 facelift came
# in May 1989 and the saloon petrol range ended in early 1994, when the Laguna
# replaced it.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Renault_21 (cited in the reference pack)
#
# Dimensions 4.462 x 1.715 x 1.415 m, wheelbase 2.600 m. Source: the reference
# pack's notes, from the Renault 21 dimension box. The hull measures 4.462 m on
# a 2.600 m wheelbase (58.3 per cent) and 1.715 m wide; mirrors extend beyond.
#
# Shape reference: no true side elevation exists. The flank was built from a
# silver UK phase-1 saloon front-left, a grey phase-1 saloon front-right and the
# silver car from the rear left, with the wheel centres fixed by the published
# ratio; comparisons were made at each photograph's angle and a true elevation
# was rendered for coherence.
#
# Colours: no British-market names were established, so the objects carry plain
# names: silver, red, blue and white. Weights silver 3, red 3, blue 2, white 2,
# total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 180 km/h, the 1.7-litre car's quoted maximum. Comfort 75/295, on the
# line 180 + 1.5 x 75: a long-legged, comfortable saloon for its class, a step
# above the 19. Classes 2,3.
#
# Dates are road presence: June 1986 intro, retires staggered 2000-2003 on a
# fourteen- to seventeen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/renault-21-phase1.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/renault-21-phase1.dae (122 objects). References:
# citycars/references/renault-21-phase1/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the lamp corners and bumper transitions are squarer than
# the photographs, the rear lamp band meets the quarter panel abruptly, and the
# body is generally more slab-sided than the real car. At 128 px the long flat
# bonnet, the slim grille and the three-box profile read as the phase-1 21.

obj=citycar
name=Renault21Phase1(Silver)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1986
intro_month=6
retire_year=2003
retire_month=6
speed=180
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=75
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=295

